---
title: Kare Raisu
description: Japanese chicken curry rice with potatoes and carrots, thickened with a homemade roux brick.
tags: [curry]
course: main
icons: [bowl-rice, carrot, drumstick]
cuisine: Japanese
source:
  name: America's Test Kitchen
  url: https://www.americastestkitchen.com/recipes/15953-kare-raisu-japanese-curry-rice-with-chicken
servings: 4
time: 1h
---

Toss the @boneless, skinless chicken thighs{1%lb}(trimmed and cut into 1-inch pieces) and @kosher salt{1%tsp} in a #bowl{}.

Heat the @vegetable oil{1%tbsp} in a #medium saucepan{} over medium heat until shimmering. Add the @onion{1}(chopped, about 1 1/4 cups) and the remaining @&kosher salt{1/4%tsp} and cook, stirring frequently, until the onion is browned, about ~brown{8%minutes}.

Add the @fresh ginger{2 1/2%tsp}(grated) and @garlic clove{1}(minced) and cook, stirring constantly, until fragrant, about ~cook{30%seconds}.

Add the chicken and cook, stirring frequently, until the chicken is no longer pink, about ~cook{3%minutes}.

Stir in the @Yukon gold potato{1%lb}(peeled and cut into 3/4-inch pieces) and @carrots{2}(peeled and cut into 1/2-inch pieces, about 1 cup). Add the @chicken broth{2 2/3%cup} and bring to a simmer over high heat. Adjust the heat to maintain a gentle simmer and cook until the potatoes are just tender, about ~simmer{20%minutes}.

Add the @./japanese-curry-roux-bricks{1/2%batch}(1 brick), @soy sauce{2%tsp}, and @Worcestershire sauce{1%tsp}, and let the block dissolve, about ~dissolve{1%minute}.

Stir gently, scraping the curry from the bottom of the pot, and simmer until the liquid thickens, about ~simmer{3%minutes}. Season with salt and pepper to taste.

Divide the @cooked Japanese short-grain rice{4%cup} evenly among 4 #shallow bowls{}, spreading it over half of each bowl. Divide the curry evenly among the bowls, making sure to ladle the curry next to the rice.

Sprinkle the @scallion{1}(sliced thin on the bias) over the curry and serve with @?fukujinzuke{} (Japanese pickles for curry), @?pickled ginger{}, or @?lemon wedges{}.
